span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Space Race Era Mage </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Wild West Promethean </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Atomic Age Promethean/Demon </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Islamic Golden Age Changeling/Mummy </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Italian Age of Revolutions Hunter/Mummy </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Third Punic War Geist </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Napoleonic Mummy </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Classical Greece Beast </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">18th Century Whaling Era Beast (yeah, shamelessly talking about Moby Dick) </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Arthurian England Mage/Beast</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T17:08:12-07:00","id":1085233,"title":"","content":"Not really sure which game line they'd be best for, but a few time-places I find interesting:<ul><li>The Weimar Republic in Germany</li> <li>The Boer Wars era in South Africa</li> <li>Hong Kong in the late 80s and early 90s at the zenith of its action movie industry</li> <li>The Republic of Texas before annexation</li> <li>The Southeastern United States before the Indian Removal Act (or right after the War of 1812)</li> <li>The Great Lakes region during the War of 1812</li> <li>England during the reign of Alfred the Great</li> <li>Oregon Country when it was jointly run by the British and United States</li> <li>The Kingdom of Aksum</li> <li>Bohemia and the Holy Roman Empire during the reign of Rudolf II</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T17:12:33-07:00","id":1085235,"title":"","content":"I would love to see them do the 1920s for all of the lines. Gatsby like Vampires, bootlegging and outlaw Werewolves, mad science and pulp adventurer Mages, and hardboiled two fisted Hunters. Mummy, Promethean and Demon already have dark eras that at least touch on this time period. Seems a natural fit for the whole CoD line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T19:05:48-07:00","id":1085275,"title":"","content":"Some of these were Eras voted upon in the first KS but I'd really love to see:<ul><li>Post-Camelot Anarchy Britain Mage</li> <li>French Revolution Mummy</li> <li>Wild West Geist</li> <li>Book of Judges Hunter</li> <li>Jazz Age Vampire</li> <li>1950s Atomic Horror Promethean/Deviant</li> <li>Meiji Restoration Werewolf</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T19:54:03-07:00","id":1085293,"title":"","content":"My thoughts:<br /> <br /> <b>Missed Kickstarter Eras</b><br /> -World's Fair Vampire<br /> -Book of Judges Hunter - It missed being in DE by three votes. You have to include it <br /> -Blitz Innocents<br /> -Wild West Geist<br /> -Orient Express Vampire<br /> -Age of Piracy Geist <br /> -Mummy/Mage French Revolution <br /> <br /> <b>Non-European/Colonial Eras</b><br /> -Xia Dynasty Vampire (China 1700 BCE)<br /> -Kipchack Werewolf (Kimek Khanate 1200-1220)<br /> -Mexican War of Independence Mage (Mexico 1810-1827)<br /> -Mana Musa's Hajj Promethean (West Africa to Arabia 1324-25)<br /> -1st Brazilian Republic Changeling (1889-1930)<br /> -Korean War Hunter (1950-1953)<br /> -Golden Horde Geist (1312-1341)<br /> -Rashidun Caliphate Mummy (Arabia 632-661)<br /> -Zulu Kingdom Demon (South Africa 1816-1828)<br /> -Zanzibar Sultanate Beast (Tanzania 1856-1964)<br /> <br /> <b>Crossovers</b> (in general, I want to see splats in crossovers actually interact, like in Mutapa and Black Death in the Companion)<br /> -Divine Comedy Geist/Promethean - Realistically Dante's Florence could host any and all game lines. I think Geist and Promethean are the closest two thematically because the Comedia keys in on the themes of Second Chances and Pilgrimage. While others may suggest focusing on Inferno (both the opening book of the Comedy and the CofD supplement) Dante is at his best if you look at all three parts of the Comedy as a whole work.<br /> -Etruscan Vampire/Mummy - Pre-Roman Vampire would be interesting, and the Etruscans practically invented Necropolises which is interesting for both Mummies and Nosferatu <br /> -Jacobite Risings Changeling/Demon - specifically on the Isle of Skye, where there are folk tales of fairies who are fallen angels. <br /> -Arthurian Mage/Changeling - Dave knows. And he knows we have. Mighty need for it. <br /> -Industrial Revolution Demon/Mummy - The God-Machine take advantage of human ingenuity while the Arisen rise to find a world that starts to resemble the one they lost lifetimes ago.<br /> <br /> <b>Others</b><br /> -Timurid Werewolf - Seconded<br /> -Cuban Revolution Vampire - Seconded <br /> -Vatican Werewolf<br /> -Red River Rebellion &amp; Northwest Rebellion Werewolf (Canada 1869 -1885) - a formative period for Western Canada and Metis culture. The importance of Louis Riel is hard to overstate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T19:55:52-07:00","id":1085294,"title":"","content":"Pretty much all the Eras that didn't win during the first KS I'd be hyped as hell for. So a couple of Eras off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> -Renaissance Italy (Mage/Promethean)<br /> -American Revolutionary War (Demon)<br /> -Edwardian England (Vampire)<br /> -Post-War Japan/Showa Era of Kaiju movies (Beast)<br /> -Khmer Rouge (Geist)<br /> -Miami Drug War (Werewolf/Hunter)","signature":"","edited"