the posts on the forum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T21:14:57-07:00","id":1085344,"title":"","content":"Qin Dynasty Vampire (with Covenants based on the Hundred Schools of Thought)<br /> <br /> French Revolution Mage (with the outbreak of the Nameless war)<br /> <br /> Haudenosaunee Hunter<br /> <br /> Dante's Italy (Geist + Inferno updates)<br /> <br /> Wild West Demon with the Unchained fleeing the Infrastructure back east to make their Hells on the frontier but it's nipping at their heels.<br /> <br /> Fifth Turn Mummy (with infinite macabre updates)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T01:22:10-07:00","id":1085395,"title":"","content":"My suggestions (for now):<br /> 1) Hunting Grounds: Sumeria - Updating the setting to 2nd Edition and expanding it (it was toooo short). Linking it to the new Werewolf history, may be as the origin of the Tribes.<br /> <br /> 2) Requiem for Rome 2nd Edition: Updating it to the revised rules, with full splats for the Julii and the Camarilla Wings.<br /> <br /> 3) Rome Awakened: A serring for Roman mages, showing the institutionalization of the Darshanas in Orders.<br /> <br /> 4) 1001 Kiths: Changeling during the Golden Age of Islam.<br /> <br /> 5) Judges Hunters: Rescuing it from the 1st DE. Biblical Hunters.<br /> <br /> 6) Spanish Civil War Geist: How would the Sin-Eaters react to the horrors of Spanish Civil War?<br /> <br /> 7) Inferno Reinassence: Infernal demons offering pacts to the Reinassance conspiracy players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T01:29:29-07:00","id":1085397,"title":"","content":"1) For Mage, definitely the Age of Piracy era - we could see the alliance between Silver Ladder and the Seers.<br /> 2) And Arthurian Mage is just too iconic not to use.<br /> <br /> 3) Also, Judges Hunter sounds amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T21:03:50-07:00","id":1085676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1085293#post1085293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> -Red River Rebellion &amp; Northwest Rebellion Werewolf (Canada 1869 -1885) - a formative period for Western Canada and Metis culture. The importance of Louis Riel is hard to overstate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't stress this enough, but Louis Riel <i>needs </i>to be in a CofD book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T21:56:23-07:00","id":1085694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1085676#post1085676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't stress this enough, but Louis Riel <i>needs </i>to be in a CofD book.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I'm actually from Winnipeg. I live there, and I love it. I'm running a Promethean game on the forums set in the city and Louis Riel has some ties to stuff in the past of my version of the CofD. A professor of mine wrote an article about why Winnipeg is so strangely Gothic, and why authors seem to congregate in the city. We have a bigger neopagan/occult scene than cities double or triple our size, I was taught the anthropology of witchcraft by a practicing witch. This place is freaking <i>weird</i>.<br /> <br /> I have <i>such </i>a hankering to see an official take on a place I know and love. Hell, if I can find the time between work and my Faculty of Education double degree program, I might try and throw my hat in the ring and do some writing myself. There's weirdness in that town, and it's been there since Louis Riel kickstarted it. Time to shed some light on it, I'd say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T22:16:06-07:00","id":1085701,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm glad to see that idea was popular. Because while I've come to love Blood Flows West from Ancient Bloodlines/Mysteries, there is so much interesting history North of the 45th parallel in that time period that people deserve to know about. And even as an Albertqn I think it should start with the Red River Rebellion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T22:34:48-07:00","id":1085705,"title":"","content":"Cross post from KS Update comment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Stole from others most ideas but added arguments why should they be in Dark Eras 2. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> First choices:<ul><li><b>Dracula's Transylvania ( 1470s-1490s CE) for Vampire</b> \u2013 I want to see creation of Ordo Dracul and Pijavica Clan \ud83d\ude0a</li> <li><b>Baptism of Poland ( 966 \u2013 1040 CE ) for Werewolf </b>\u2013 Need to promote interesting times of my nation when pagan clashed with Christanity. \ud83d\ude0a</li> <li><b>Beast of Gevaudan ( 1760s CE ) France for Werewolf</b> - Just rewatched Brotherhood of Wolf \ud83d\ude0a</li> <li><b>Creation of Roman Empire ( 44 BCE \u2013 27 BCE ) for Mage</b> \u2013 We need to see the start of Diamond and Seers of Throne s Orders from Darshanas and have Roman Era for all Big Three! All in background of rise to power for Augustus Caesar! \ud83d\ude0a</li> <li><b>England\u2019s Anarchy War ( 1135 - 1153 CE ) for Mage</b> \u2013 I want to see this Camelot as Time Before and write-ups of Keepers of Word, Panscryptias and Tremere as Orders! \ud83d\ude09</li> <li><b>USSR (first nuclear tests in 1950's CE ) for Promethean &amp; Deviant</b> ( if will be then )\u2013 We need Zeka! \ud83d\ude0a</li> <li><b>1001 Kiths: Golden Age of Islam ( 786 to 1258 CE ) for Changeling</b> \u2013 And writing of 1001 Nights \ud83d\ude0a</li> <li><b>Mughal Empire ( 1526\u20131540 CE ) in India for Hunter</b></li> <li><b>Mongol Invasions of Europe ( 1206\u20131337 CE ) for Beast</b></li> <li><b>London Blitz ( 1940-1941 CE ) for Innocents</b> ( playing children against monsters and war \ud83d\ude0a )</li> </ul>Second choices:<ul><li><b>French Revolution ( 1789 - 1799 CE ) for Mage &amp; Beast </b>\u2013 Need to see Reign of Horrors ( \ud83d\ude09 ) and start of Nameless War</li> <li><b>Golden Age of Piracy (1650s to 1730s CE) for Mage &amp; Geist </b> \u2013 Need to see this Silver Ladder and Seers of Throne alliance against Nameless Order in Pirates Republic of Nassau. \ud83d\ude0a</li> <li><b>The Nameless War ( whole XIX century CE ) for Mage</b> \u2013 But probably outside of Dark Eras chapter scope... \u2639</li> <li><b>Age of Discovery ( XV to XVIII century CE ) for Mage &amp; Beast</b> \u2013 Wonders and terrors of New Worlds discovered \ud83d\ude0a</li> <li><b>Meiji Restoration ( circa 1868 CE ) for Werewolf </b></li> <li><b>Spanish Inquisition ( 1478 to 1502 CE ) for Hunter </b></li> <li><b>Roman Britain ( somewhere 43 to 410 CE ) for Changeling </b></li> <li><b>Bronze Age Collapse (1200 - 1100 BCE) for Werewolf </b>- to pick up from teasers in Forsaken by Rome) \ud83d\ude03</li> <li><b>Vatican Werewolf \u2013 problems with Papcy</b></li> <li><b>Height of Babylon for Geist &amp; Mage</b></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-30-2017, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T01:59:48-07:00","id":1085739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1085694#post1085694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I'm actually from Winnipeg. I live there, and I love it. I'm running a Promethean game on the forums set in the city and Louis Riel has some ties to stuff in the past of my version of the CofD. A professor of mine wrote an article about why Winnipeg is so strangely Gothic, and why authors seem to congregate in the city. We have a bigger neopagan/occult scene than cities double or triple our size, I was taught the anthropology of witchcraft by a practicing witch. This place is freaking <i>weird</i>.<br /> <br /> I have <i>such </i>a hankering to see an official take on a place I know and love. Hell, if I can find the time between work and my Faculty of Education double degree program, I might try and throw my hat in the ring and do some writing myself. There's weirdness in that town, and it's been there since Louis Riel kickstarted it. Time to shed some light on it, I'd say.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the same vein, I feel like the Guy Maddin aesthetic has a place in CofD, too. <i>My Winnipeg</i>, indeed.<br /> <br /> (The general strike would be pretty interesting too.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 04-30-2017, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T03:09:41-07:00","id":1085743,"title":"","content":"Going to plug it again:<br /> <br /> Dark Eras: The Electroweak Epoch.<br /> <br /> Building on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/563946-if-you-controlled-dark-eras-2?p=564730#post564730\">malonkey1</a>'s suggestion:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>New Line Proposal</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For eons the quanta have lived a life of ease, choosing whatever path they deemed suited their lifestyle. Now however the universe has gone cold and dark beings known only as &quot;The Observers&quot; seek to lock down the quanta to one classical life path. Join the quanta as they use all the punk outrage they can summon against determinism in Onyx Path's Muon: the Collision</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T11:01:01-07:00","id":1085826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1085294#post1085294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much all the Eras that didn't win during the first KS I'd be hyped as hell for. So a couple of Eras off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> <br /> -Post-War Japan/Showa Era of Kaiju movies (Beast)<br /> -Miami Drug War (Werewolf/Hunter)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! Godzilla as a begotten AND 80s coke dealer werewolves. YES!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T11:33:33-07:00","id":1085836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1085395#post1085395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Requiem for Rome 2nd Edition: Updating it to the revised rules, with full splats for the Julii and the Camarilla Wings.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offence, but desperately do not want to see this, and would be bitterly disappointed if OPP went this route. The best part of Dark Eras is learning something new. The Julil are apparently being updated in Thousand Years of Night. I'd much rather see the an era focusing on the Etruscans, Roman Greece, Caesarian Britain, Parthia, or the legions that supposedly got sold into slavery in China. Update the Wings there. That at least adds something new to the narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T13:29:30-07:00","id":1085866,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see the Axis occupation of Greece (1941 - 1945). I could see it for any game line, although Demon, Geist, or Werewolf would probably work well. <br /> <br /> Also, I have to suggest the Dancing Plague of 1518. I don't care which game line it's for, I just think it would be interesting to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T13:50:01-07:00","id":1085878,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see the time leading up to the exclusion of the Tremere from the Diamond. Not the event itself, but rather see what role the Tremere had in the Diamond, and what the other Orders were like before a fifth of the Diamond were excommunicated en masse.<br /> I realise it's not tied to any real historic event, but it's such a huge part of Mage history that I think it needs a dedicated word count.<br /> But I'm also a bit cautious about asking for it since I'd prefer to have 2E rules for Tremere either in that Era or published beforehand, and I'm not sure that's going to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T14:03:37-07:00","id":1085881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1085878#post1085878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see the time leading up to the exclusion of the Tremere from the Diamond. Not the event itself, but rather see what role the Tremere had in the Diamond, and what the other Orders were like before a fifth of the Diamond were excommunicated en masse.<br /> I realise it's not tied to any real historic event, but it's such a huge part of Mage history that I think it needs a dedicated word count.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you want <b>Britain's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Anarchy\" target=\"_blank\"><i>The Anarchy</i> War</a> Era</b> that <b>DaveB</b> mentioned few times around on forum he want to write - it's in years 1135 - 1153 CE, so only few decades before full excommunication of Tremere from Diamond. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's also times of great revolt in England, 'English man vs previous Vikings' war, of massive 'Camelot' research in Awakened circles and 'last stand' of Pancryptias vs Keepers of Word race before merge into Mysterium. Plus, <b>Mage</b> Era in Middle Ages, man! We need this, for Oracle sake! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-30-2017, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T14:07:19-07:00","id":1085882,"title":"","content":"As someone with a deep background in history, all I can say is that there are so many eras simply rife with possibilities. 1920s/30s Shanghai with its international vibe playing against nascent nationalism ... 1730s-80s Europe with the Age of Enlightenment crashing into secret societies and the Cult of Sensibility ... Norman Sicily with its wash of cultures ... basically any era where you suddenly get a melding or clashing of wildly different cultures ... simply add one or mire aspects of Chronicles of Darkness and stir liberally. And, yes, I think some of the &quot;newer&quot; lines (Beast, Demon, Mummy) need to be emphasized. <br /> <br /> I will admit that I am always a bit hesitant abiut Arthurian settings, simply because it is more of a concept than a true time period. Depending on one's vision of King Arthur, this could be anything from 4th century Britain as a whole, subsections such as the West Country, Wales, or even southern Scotland, or even Brittany (Less Britain) as late as the 10th century, possibly with overlays of the 15th. OTOH, there was a strong tradition of interaction between the tales as written (beginning in the 12th century) and courtly culture. Characters of the tales in contemporary clothing and armour ... then courtiers ape the actions of the books, inclufing costume revels and tournaments... leading to a new round of tales in the now-contemporary costumes and armour ... lather, rinse, repeat. Hmm ... maybe this is involvement by the Fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T14:12:25-07:00","id":1085885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1085294#post1085294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Miami Drug War (Werewolf/Hunter)</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember reading Carl Hiaasen's columns in the Miami Herald from the mid 80s. The movie Scarface barely scratched the surface of how crazy, corrupt and violent the city was in the late 70s and early 80s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T14:19:32-07:00","id":1085888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MhicWombat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1085882#post1085882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will admit that I am always a bit hesitant abiut Arthurian settings, simply because it is more of a concept than a true time period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arthurian 'Camelot' in <b>Mage</b> is canoniclly name for Britain's local Time Before places and items, just like in Mediterranean Sea area ( Greece, Rome and Egypt ) they where called 'Atlantis'. Merlin is canonical Silver Ladder Acanthus that used myths and those connection to Ascended and show middle finger to Exarchs. But 'Camelot' is only as much viable as 'Atlantis' is - it can be local variant of Awakened Society, or they both could be pieces of the same UrCivilization, from the dawn of times. <b>DaveB</b> even wrote he wanted to write some alternative setting with Camelot being real place character could be possible to enter - but changed mind as it would not work in <b>CoD</b> universe as it is.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot\">Whole topic on Camelot</a> in <b>Mage</b>. And most important quotes from <b>DaveB</b> on matter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=40121#post40121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Merlin created a Utopia using long-term manipulations of Fate and Destiny as his Omens - his Noumenon was to establish a destined link between a king and the land, and he Ascended (his body turning into the crystal cave) when the Bane of all those destinies came true.<br /> <br /> At which point, the whole damn thing was promptly erased from the timeline by the Ruin. But no matter what the Exarchs do, Arthurian symbols resonate with the Acanthus, and the Aeon of Fate transformed from the Greek Triple-Fates into Mordred.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=41589#post41589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, and I feel okay with telling you this, but that setting was the one of the two I came up with for Dark Eras that we <i>didn't</i> end up writing.<br /> <br /> Dark Ages Britain, replacing &quot;Atlantis&quot; with &quot;Arthurian Britain&quot; as the origin for the inexplicable mysteries and stripping all the Romantic era additions from the myths. It'd be Arthurian as in &quot;grinning blood-soaked warlord&quot; Arthur, stone circles built by giants, probably-not-allegorical dragons, remnants of the old religion, pugnacious Christian saints and all.<br /> <br /> Just like Atlantis never happened in the modern-day setting but mages encounter evidence of it, the setting would be the real Dark Ages - and unlike other games we've made in the past would <i>actually</i> be set in the Dark Ages, not several centuries later - but with the ahistorical magical remnants of Arthurian Britain poking up from the seams.<br /> <br /> Naturally, a few days after I pitched it I found a FATE game called Age of Arthur that hits the same &quot;anti-Pendragon&quot; spot I was aiming for. C'est La Vie. The setting that won out for Dark Eras is more &quot;a very interesting period from Awakening's history that highlights its themes&quot; than &quot;Awakening's themes transplanted to an alien time, largely disconnected from the gameline&quot;, so I believe we've made the right decision.<br /> <br /> Camelot will just go on being an occassionally-mentioned cool bit in Awakening's setting lore.<br /> <br /> It's cropped up recently in our discussions for Fallen World Chronicle, actually. We were talking about how we want the Acanthus to shift in presentation from &quot;effortless and unconcerned&quot; to &quot;schemers who see possible futures and then manipulate events to go down their preferred ones&quot; - passive characters to proactive ones. The first two exemples of characters we're thinking of for the nuAcanthus? Paul Mau'dib from Dune... And Merlin.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-30-2017, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T14:58:06-07:00","id":1085905,"title":"","content":"While I think that British Mage setting would be cool, I think we''ll get to see a lot of history in Tome of the Pentacle. It'll be a different presentation than a Dark Era but we'll still get to delve into the Tremere being part of polite society and the Nameless War. Maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T15:08:29-07:00","id":1085907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1085905#post1085905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I think that British Mage setting would be cool, I think we''ll get to see a lot of history in Tome of the Pentacle. It'll be a different presentation than a Dark Era but we'll still get to delve into the Tremere being part of polite society and the Nameless War. Maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read any summary of what the book will be about, but the title implies that any historical focus would start with the Nameless War, while the Tremere were excluded around 700 years prior to that, with potential mentions serving to provide context for more recent history.<br /> <br /> Is there a summary that I can read anywhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T17:09:11-07:00","id":1085951,"title":"","content":"I'm only speculating, but the Orders were well established during that period and technically were a Pentacle since the Mysterium was separated into two Orders for most of that time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T21:38:53-07:00","id":1086063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1085836#post1085836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No offence, but desperately do not want to see this, and would be bitterly disappointed if OPP went this route. The best part of Dark Eras is learning something new. The Julil are apparently being updated in Thousand Years of Night. I'd much rather see the an era focusing on the Etruscans, Roman Greece, Caesarian Britain, Parthia, or the legions that supposedly got sold into slavery in China. Update the Wings there. That at least adds something new to the narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, youre right. When I say updating Requiem for Rome, I mean updating its mechanics, but not necessarily the same setting. It could be another different Roman setting, as the Triunvirate and the end of the Republic (with the Camarilla Propinqui divided in supporting Caesar, Crassus, Pompey or the Senate), or the Punic Wars. Or a Punic, Persian or Parthian setting with the roman updating in a sidebar.<br /> <br /> Or even better, the Roman Monarchy: show us how Rome was during the Stirges Rule, with Roman Propinqui as their servants. That would offer us a totally distinct vampire setting, as the Strix as ruling class. It could be during the last days of the monarchy, with the Julius Senex rebelion as a history seed, for instance. And although it's pre Camarilla, it could offer us the updated rules for the wings in the &quot;What Is to Come&quot; section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 05-01-2017, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T21:41:11-07:00","id":1086066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1085885#post1085885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember reading Carl Hiaasen's columns in the Miami Herald from the mid 80s. The movie Scarface barely scratched the surface of how crazy, corrupt and violent the city was in the late 70s and early 80s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Splat should get an 80s era<br /> <br /> werewolf and geist for drug wars and youth culture/latch key kid related panics of the era(and the birth of the goth scene for Geist), which leads into... Beast, changeling, and maybe hunter for satanic panic and mage and demon for the rapid technological progress of that era and it's effects on society and the american astral realm.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T23:07:15-07:00","id":1086080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1085951#post1085951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm only speculating, but the Orders were well established during that period and technically were a Pentacle since the Mysterium was separated into two Orders for most of that time</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpicks - Pentacle was created when Free Council joined Diamond in 20th century, after Council of Free Assemblies creation - before it all, it was still only Diamond Orders. Mysterium was created in 12th century and starts to propagate Panscryptias and Keepers of Word union in Byzantine Empire. And small correction on Tremere excommunication - it was in year 1099 in Convocation of Antioch, so in 1150s in Britain they still can be okay, as spreading 'we must ban Tremere as Diamond Order' may take some time.<br /> <br /> <b>So our Britain's Anarchy Dark Era (1135 - 1153 CE) is even more interesting</b> - it's time when in Britain last Panscryptias and Keepers of Word are still as separate Orders, but only on Isles. On the other hand, Tremere are banned as Order all around Europe and ban is slowly coming to Britain - but it's literal Anarchy in kingdom so Liches are here spreading in 'last bastion' kind a thing! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-01-2017, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T04:06:28-07:00","id":1086125,"title":"","content":"Well, I said the Orders were well established as in four of the five so my nitpick is that I wasn't wrong. I know the Mysterium was created from the union of two Orders, as I did mention that. I'm not sure what correction you're making regarding Tremere excommunication because I never gave a date and implied that it was early medieval (or at least post-Roman) anyway.<br /> <br /> I knew all the facts in your nitpick already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T15:38:25-07:00","id":1086364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1085826#post1085826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes! Godzilla as a begotten AND 80s coke dealer werewolves. YES!</div> </div> </div> </div>The original Godzilla movie WAS meant to be a cautionary tale on, not just nuclear devastation, but on unchecked scientific progress. Helluva lesson to be taught. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1085885#post1085885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading Carl Hiaasen's columns in the Miami Herald from the mid 80s. The movie Scarface barely scratched the surface of how crazy, corrupt and violent the city was in the late 70s and early 80s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah.<br /> <br /> Multiple criminal organizations pushing into one city and clashes with law enforcement, often violently, would have the local Forsaken working overtime: territory violations and encroachments, the number of violence, drug, decadence, and greed spirits being attracted to the mess, and human and Wolf-Blooded allies being caught in the crossfire.<br /> <br /> Also for hunters, with all the violence, them knowing full well that all the supernatural entities would use the drug wars as cover to do their business. Or being called in as specialists for particularly unusual deaths and killings. And that all the violence could be enough to bring about any local Slashers.<br /> <br /> Which speaking of: the 1980's were the golden age of Slasher movies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T16:02:37-07:00","id":1086374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1086364#post1086364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also for hunters, with all the violence, them knowing full well that all the supernatural entities would use the drug wars as cover to do their business. Or being called in as specialists for particularly unusual deaths and killings. And that all the violence could be enough to bring about any local Slashers.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that is in fact the origin of Jeff Lindsay's Dexter Morgan character. <br /> <br /> Clearly such a setting needs some sort of urban legend boogieman who goes about murdering cocaine cowboys in motel bathrooms with a chainsaw. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T16:30:55-07:00","id":1086379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1086374#post1086374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly such a setting needs some sort of urban legend boogieman who goes about murdering cocaine cowboys in motel bathrooms with a chainsaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>...so Jacket from the Hotline Miami games? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Which was actually the other thing I had in mind when thinking on Slashers and the Miami Drug War. You get Hotline Miami. And it would make for an interesting chronicle for a cell of hunters having to stop this bloodthirsty, out of control Slasher that's just killing EVERYONE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T17:25:04-07:00","id":1086390,"title":"","content":"Okay so for the 80s we have<br /> <br /> Werewolf= Drug Wars<br /> <br /> Mage = Technological changes and their effect on the american society / astral<br /> <br /> changeling = ?<br /> <br /> Hunter = Golden Age of Slashers<br /> <br /> Beast/inferno (Inferno suggested by Malonkey) = Satanic Panic<br /> <br /> Geist = ?<br /> <br /> Demon = 19