div> </div> </div> </div>YES! Given how many empires Afghanistan has ended, it would be nice to how the arisen view the Vietnam of the USSR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T08:17:45-07:00","id":1086645,"title":"","content":"I definitely back bring back the era that didn't quite make it like Golden Age of Piracy and Wild West Geist.<br /> <br /> Perhaps 1960s-1970s Aokigahara, Japan for Geist when the site rose in popularity after the 1960's Novel Kuroi Jukai came out and there were annual body searches in the 70s for the forest? It does have a reputation of being haunted by yurei.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T17:00:15-07:00","id":1086883,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>Beast/Inferno during the Satanic Panic of the 80s/90s: Heroes are getting free reign to persecute Beasts under the guise of seeking out &quot;satanic abusers,&quot; While the few real demonic cults are working in the shadows.</li> <li>Cold War Deviant: The Cold War is escalating, and both sides have taken to mixing weapon and soldier, often without getting permission from their subjects. Will you stay loyal to your country, defect to the other side, or hide from both?</li> <li>Sengoku Jidai Werewolf: Japan has fallen into countless warring states, making the job of protecting the Shadow and the Physical from each other even <i>more</i> difficult as spirits of war and violence grow fat, especially when some packs have chosen to take sides in the conflict.</li> <li>Ancient Greek Hunter/Beast: In a time of myth and legend. When the ancient gods were petty and cruel, and they plagued mankind with suffering, few had the strength to challenge their power.</li> <li>A single World War II Super-Era for every line</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T04:36:41-07:00","id":1087101,"title":"","content":"(Sorry, should have posted in this thread instead)<br /> <br /> I humbly submit these for Backers to consider: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Werewolf/Hunter: Baltic Crusades, Livonian and Prussian specifically.</li> <li>Inferno: Early Protestant Reformation in England and Germany.</li> <li>Mage/Promethean: Prague during reign of Rudolph II.</li> <li>Mage: Late 18th century Bavaria.</li> <li>Werewolf: French and Indian War.</li> <li>Vampire/Hunter: Prohibition era New York/Chicago.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> I had written more detailed explanations about each one but my browser crashed and I can't be bothered to write them out again now, maybe later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T17:45:07-07:00","id":1087419,"title":"","content":"I feel like some of the suggestions being made are ridiculously specific. I hope they settle on ones that are broader in scope and theme, that are more than just: &quot;this splat during this event&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T18:01:39-07:00","id":1087430,"title":"","content":"My suggestion, wait till the core books are updated, otherwise you'll end up with another mechanical mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T20:26:07-07:00","id":1087489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1086883#post1086883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Beast/Inferno during the Satanic Panic of the 80s/90s: Heroes are getting free reign to persecute Beasts under the guise of seeking out &quot;satanic abusers,&quot; While the few real demonic cults are working in the shadows.</li> <li>Cold War Deviant: The Cold War is escalating, and both sides have taken to mixing weapon and soldier, often without getting permission from their subjects. Will you stay loyal to your country, defect to the other side, or hide from both?</li> <li>Sengoku Jidai Werewolf: Japan has fallen into countless warring states, making the job of protecting the Shadow and the Physical from each other even <i>more</i> difficult as spirits of war and violence grow fat, especially when some packs have chosen to take sides in the conflict.</li> <li>Ancient Greek Hunter/Beast: In a time of myth and legend. When the ancient gods were petty and cruel, and they plagued mankind with suffering, few had the strength to challenge their power.</li> <li>A single World War II Super-Era for every line</li> </ul><br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Why didn't I think of involving inferno? Also, going that route should probably include drawing a connection between the prosperity gospel that was (and still is) the favorite of the televangelists and Mammon's domain of Greed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T20:47:50-07:00","id":1087496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1087489#post1087489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why didn't I think of involving inferno? Also, going that route should probably include drawing a connection between the prosperity gospel that was (and still is) the favorite of the televangelists and Mammon's domain of Greed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T00:40:14-07:00","id":1087558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1087430#post1087430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My suggestion, wait till the core books are updated, otherwise you'll end up with another mechanical mess.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This isn't constructive or in the spirit of the thread. This is thread crapping don't do it again, you are getting out of hand with the negative posts in any DE related threads.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T01:59:22-07:00","id":1087577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1087489#post1087489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why didn't I think of involving inferno? Also, going that route should probably include drawing a connection between the prosperity gospel that was (and still is) the favorite of the televangelists and Mammon's domain of Greed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would prefer an era soley focussed on Inferno, give the devs a bit more space to reintroduce the inferno demons without having to create a whole new book for 2E just yet. Not that I would mind a whole 2E Inferno, the fact that it was incompatible with 2E is what put me off 2E for so long.<br /> <br /> A few more I thought to add to my previous post:<br /> <br /> Beast: Carolingian Empire, the Kingdom of Charlemagne.<br /> Beast: Mayan Empire<br /> Immortals: Early 20th Century US eugenics craze.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T04:43:07-07:00","id":1087623,"title":"","content":"Jejakabhukti: 9th to 13th centuries. Changeling/Beast. <br /> <br /> Irem: Mummy/Mage<br /> <br /> The Cruasades: Inferno/Demon the Descent<br /> <br /> Haitian Revolution: Mages/Giests<br /> <br /> Caanan: Demon/Changeling<br /> <br /> Newfoundland joining Canada: Werewolf<br /> <br /> Moorish Spain: Vampire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T12:46:07-07:00","id":1087865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1087577#post1087577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would prefer an era solely focused on Inferno, give the devs a bit more space to reintroduce the inferno demons without having to create a whole new book for 2E just yet. Not that I would mind a whole 2E Inferno, the fact that it was incompatible with 2E is what put me off 2E for so long.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, the satanic panic was above all else, a moral panic driven by fears about the direction of american society, the fact that real Satanists were really just some edgy Ayn Rand fans should be reflected in the Dark Era, the real &quot;satanists&quot; were the &quot;greed is good&quot; types, including the televangelists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T13:37:55-07:00","id":1087895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1087865#post1087865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree, the satanic panic was above all else, a moral panic driven by fears about the direction of american society, the fact that real Satanists were really just some edgy Ayn Rand fans should be reflected in the Dark Era, the real &quot;satanists&quot; were the &quot;greed is good&quot; types, including the televangelists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that makes sense, my only real knowledge of the Satanic Panic is from that one X-Files episode. I guess some of the really nasty Wall Street Crashes would also be a good place to explore the theme of Greed.<br /> <br /> That's also partly why I suggested the Reformation, both sides of it accused the other of being under infernal influence, Protestants viewed the Pope as the living Antichrist on earth and the Catholics saw the Protestants as heretics in league with the Devil. It led to intense hatred, which resulted in the burning of heretics, the seizure of Church lands by Protestant rulers, (they were worth a lot of money, you see, and harbored riches donated by believers) bloody peasants wars and the start of a very long &quot;cold war&quot; between Catholic Spain and Protestant England. It was basically the religious paranoia you described, but on two opposing sides and far more violent, perfect and thematically appropriate feeding ground for inferno demons.<br /> <br /> Appropriately enough that's also round about the time the legend of Dr. Faustus became a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T14:28:21-07:00","id":1087916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1087895#post1087895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess that makes sense, my only real knowledge of the Satanic Panic is from that one X-Files episode. I guess some of the really nasty Wall Street Crashes would also be a good place to explore the theme of Greed.<br /> <br /> That's also partly why I suggested the Reformation, both sides of it accused the other of being under infernal influence, Protestants viewed the Pope as the living Antichrist on earth and the Catholics saw the Protestants as heretics in league with the Devil. It led to intense hatred, which resulted in the burning of heretics, the seizure of Church lands by Protestant rulers, (they were worth a lot of money, you see, and harbored riches donated by believers) bloody peasants wars and the start of a very long &quot;cold war&quot; between Catholic Spain and Protestant England. It was basically the religious paranoia you described, but on two opposing sides and far more violent, perfect and thematically appropriate feeding ground for inferno demons.<br /> <br /> Appropriately enough that's also round about the time the legend of Dr. Faustus became a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in that case, two books you really need to read on the subject are S<a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Satans-Silence-Ritual-Making-American/dp/0595189555\" target=\"_blank\">atan's Silence </a>and <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/We-Believe-Children-Moral-Panic/dp/1610392876\" target=\"_blank\">We Believe the Children</a>: A Moral Panic in the 1980s. together the two books do a good job of explaining how the panic was the result of a combination of cultural anxiety about the changing role of women in society and the home, heightened awareness of sexual abuse,corrosive interviewing techniques of children by social workers and police, prosecutors who wanted to become famous by busting a satanic cult, the rise of the religious right and the resulting culture wars, and opportunistic media who used lurid tales of satanic cults to boost ratings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T18:04:25-07:00","id":1088024,"title":"","content":"After it scored a few brief mentions in Promethean, I'd be real interested in an Antarctic Dark Era. Specifically during the very first years of the 20th Century, the age of Scott and Shackleton and Amundsen. While Promethean might work, I actually kind of prefer the idea of it being a Mortals Dark Era. Themes of isolation and discovering the world is a darker and more dangerous place than you know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1087623#post1087623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irem: Mummy/Mage</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a Mortals/Mage Crossover, strictly speaking <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Although I am seriously wary of the idea of one splat being involved in the creation mythology of another.<br /> <br /> It's also a fictional era. I can't help but feel like it would be better suited for a Mummy expansion delving into the game's mythology than a Dark Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T18:14:26-07:00","id":1088029,"title":"","content":"It might be a blue book due to the lack of actual mummies, but I do agree that it could be the basis for an entire book. I mean VtR in Rome got two books; Requiem for Rome and Fall of the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T23:31:42-07:00","id":1088125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1088024#post1088024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be a Mortals/Mage Crossover, strictly speaking <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Although I am seriously wary of the idea of one splat being involved in the creation mythology of another.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's exactly what's being proposed. There's already a degree of crossover. Irem goes to war with an empire in Mesopotamia which reading between the lines you could see corresponding to Kish (or is it Kush?), which is a Scelesti city mentioned in Left-Hand Path. It's a pretty big deal in the history of Awakening's setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T00:04:59-07:00","id":1088129,"title":"","content":"Having watched the latest season of Archer maybe a Demon or Changeling Los Angeles late 40's early 50's setting is in order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T00:43:40-07:00","id":1088135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1088129#post1088129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having watched the latest season of Archer maybe a Demon or Changeling Los Angeles late 40's early 50's setting is in order.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Notably they already did Mage Noir for the late 40s being done there (complete with the focus on WW2 vets with PTSD).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T01:56:49-07:00","id":1088152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1088125#post1088125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that's exactly what's being proposed. There's already a degree of crossover. Irem goes to war with an empire in Mesopotamia which reading between the lines you could see corresponding to Kish (or is it Kush?), which is a Scelesti city mentioned in Left-Hand Path. It's a pretty big deal in the history of Awakening's setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between implication and hints that allow players to make up their own minds on the subject and having the first definitive exploration of the Arisen's origins prominently feature another splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T03:13:44-07:00","id":1088170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks#post1085120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own suggestions:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Dracula's Transylvania for Vampire. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about the time the original novel was set and written, or the period of Vlad Tepes? If it\u2019s the former a good period would be the Austro-Hungarian Empire from around 1880 to about 1910. If it\u2019s the latter, it should probably be the Ottoman\u2013Hungarian wars focused around the mid-1400s.<br /> <br /> Can someone also clarify, will there be a separate Dark Eras 2 Kickstarter to donate to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T07:05:55-07:00","id":1088267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1088152#post1088152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a difference between implication and hints that allow players to make up their own minds on the subject and having the first definitive exploration of the Arisen's origins prominently feature another splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not that big an influence really. Irem and the Ki-En-Gir go to war, and then make a peace settlement, that's kinda it. They're just two important periods which happen to coincide.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T12:30:10-07:00","id":1088422,"title":"","content":"Actually, I think that Dave have stated that the Ki En Gir were Scelesti, and that the war between the two empires was the first (or one of the first) example of forces from the Lower Depths and the Abyss killing each other, at least in massive scale. I can't track the quote, and at any way it can't be considered canon, but it does fit everything we know about the time and place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T12:59:40-07:00","id":1088436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1088422#post1088422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I think that Dave have stated that the Ki En Gir were Scelesti, and that the war between the two empires was the first (or one of the first) example of forces from the Lower Depths and the Abyss killing each other, at least in massive scale. I can't track the quote, and at any way it can't be considered canon, but it does fit everything we know about the time and place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here you go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=971430#post971430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, the earliest historical (not prehistorical, pre-Sundering, like the vinca; first people anyone's heard of) societies of mages were based in Kish, and were what modern Awakened would call Scelesti. They worshipped the Abyss, summoned legions of Gulmoth, and had a nice big war with a certain other Near-East ancient superpower (Irem vs Kish: the first major example of Lower Depths-fuelled things having a grudge match with Abyss-fuelled things!)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T03:37:33-07:00","id":1088683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1088267#post1088267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're not that big an influence really. Irem and the Ki-En-Gir go to war, and then make a peace settlement, that's kinda it. They're just two important periods which happen to coincide.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm getting at is that, by default, the forces of Ki-En-Gir are just Sekhem Sorcerers. They're only Mages if you play crossover. Releasing a Dark Era that definitively adds the presence of another game line into the heart of Mummy's creation story is not something that meshes well in my mind with the sandbox nature of World of Darkness. The modular, sandbox nature of the setting works better when you can choose to weave hints and inferences together to create crossover timelines and cosmologies, rather than beginning with those crossovers in place and making, say, a Mummy player have to wade through a whole lot of information on an irrelevant game line to find out what Irem was actually like.<br /> <br /> Plus, Ki-En-Gir is not a small part of the Mummy creation story. They did not just go to war, then make a peace settlement. The Shan'iatu obliterated the civilisation in order to feed Ammut and draw from her the knowledge required to fuel the Rite of Return. Its annihilation was what allowed the creation of the Arisen to begin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T10:42:02-07:00","id":1088796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I'm getting at is that, by default, the forces of Ki-En-Gir are just Sekhem Sorcerers. </div> </div> </div>No they're not. They're different. That's the entire point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1088683#post1088683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, Ki-En-Gir is not a small part of the Mummy creation story. They did not just go to war, then make a peace settlement. The Shan'iatu obliterated the civilisation in order to feed Ammut and draw from her the knowledge required to fuel the Rite of Return. Its annihilation was what allowed the creation of the Arisen to begin.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's confusingly written but they didn't. They destroyed the citadel of Ubar. Plus, Ki-En-Gir isn't fictional, it's Sumer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T15:48:52-07:00","id":1088885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1088170#post1088170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you talking about the time the original novel was set and written, or the period of Vlad Tepes? If it\u2019s the former a good period would be the Austro-Hungarian Empire from around 1880 to about 1910. If it\u2019s the latter, it should probably be the Ottoman\u2013Hungarian wars focused around the mid-1400s.<br /> <br /> Can someone also clarify, will there be a separate Dark Eras 2 Kickstarter to donate to?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was thinking move Vlad, both are good ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T15:49:39-07:00","id":1088887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1088796#post1088796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No they're not. They're different. That's the entire point.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the core book calls them seers, oracles, and mystics (all powers that are actually theoretically possible under the Sekhem Sorcerer rules), they are described in Lore of the Deceived as &quot;sorcerers and relic-makers&quot;. I get that it looks like a cute shout-out to Mage with those references, and it certainly can mean what you want it to mean, but that's the point of the sandbox nature of these games. References to other game lines can mean them if you want those game lines to exist in your setting, but I can't say I see definitive declarations of, &quot;Yes, this other splat plays a core part in this other splat's world&quot; very often. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085120-call-for-suggestions-for-dark-eras-2-in-the-latest-update-for-the-original-ks?p=1088796#post1088796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's confusingly written but they didn't. They destroyed the citadel of Ubar. Plus, Ki-En-Gir isn't fictional, it's Sumer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really my point, although I apologise for getting that wrong. I double-checked, and yes, they destroy Ubar, and subjugate Ki-En-Gir. <br /> <br /> However, what I was taking issue with was the significance of the event. It's not, &quot;Go to war, make peace, kinda it&quot;. It's &quot;go to war, kill the king, desecrate his body, bathe an entire fortress in such slaughter that it acts as tribute to Ammut and sees the entire place removed from the face of the planet, get the knowledge of the Rite of Return in exchange&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T20:21:04-07:00","id":1088978,"title":"","content":"Sumerian Promethean.<br /> Punic Wars-era Carthage Hunter.<br /> Just barely pre-Columbus North American Geist.<br /> Spanish Inquisition Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T06:23:32-07:00","id":1089097,"title":"","content":"Kish vs. Irem war would be interesting and lets be honest Mages, Changelings, Werewolves, and Vampires would be found in Irem like anyother place.<br /> <br /> It being the first war between the Abyss and the Lower Depths makes it really interesting.<br /> <br /> And its not the first set of splats to interact on that level, the actions of the Firstborn in taking down Father Wolf had a huge effect on Mages and their cosmology, and Father Wolf and the Firstborn (and maybe some or all of the Idigam) had Arcana!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T06:49:28-07:00","id":1089114,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">While I'd like to see more Italy in CofD, Ancient Rome and Renaissance are the easiest choices... I'd take them, but I think there are other options. Just a few examples:<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 VIII-396 B.C, Etruria vs early Rome [Vampire/Mage/Geist]: </b>Second Chances already suggested it and I was like &quot;YES&quot;. Ok, ok, I said no Ancient Rome... but Rome in this case is a footnote. Rome in this era would be at first &quot;that annoying neighbor&quot;, then &quot;that city we ruled for a while&quot; and in the end &quot;THE ENEMY&quot;. I don't know how much is said, if at all, about the Etruscans in Mage but I think we are still in a time where mages haven't figured magic out, like, at all. Mages know bits and pieces, and only encounters with different civilizations help them getting the puzzle together. At the beginning Romans, and Latins, know probably just a little more than the Awakened from the Sundered World. Etruscans are way more ahead: they have had many more contacts with the Greeks from Magna Grecia, and are probably versed in divination and all things Death (but why is there a huge concentration of Moros in Etruria?). Vampires are there for the obvious links with Requiem for Rome without actually being RfR, and Geist because... just because. Death.<br /> <b>\u2022 1870-1881 Post-Indipendence Italy [Promethean]:</b>In 1861, Italy finally becomes one. But what it means being a country? What happens when you don't have a singular language and your newfound population doesn't think of itself as Italian, and it's dirt poor? In this era, Italy is trying to find itself, and fails. And it will continue to fail for generations. I think it's a nice parallel for the Promethean condition. It's a struggle for the right of existing as oneself. Also, 1880 is the year of publication of <i>The Malavoglia</i> (it's completely mundane, no supernatural at all, but it's really in theme) and 1881 is the one of Pinocchio, who, in my headcanon, is an Extempore, the only one who reached the New Dawn.<br /> <b>\u2022 1943-1944, Nazi Occupation of Rome [Werewolf]</b>: I don't know how feasible it is, since, y'know, Nazi are kind of a touchy subject (understatement of the year). I'd like to see the occupation more &quot;in the background&quot;. The main characters are trying to survive, and making their packs' life less miserable, more than just trying to force the hand of the Resistance. The USA were dropping bombs, the Nazi were doing what Nazi do, the Pope was silent... not a good time for the Shadow. There may be Wounds as big as entire neighborhoods.<br /> <b>\u2022 1950-1969, Post-War Italy [Mage/(Mummy)]:</b> A way more hopeful era. The country was reinventing itself, TVs were getting more popular, making finally a unified Italian popular culture possible (Italy is, like, 150 years old). It was living an economic boom... but only in the North. More and more people from the South were emigrating to the North, especially to Turin, where the FIAT factories were at their greatest. Prejudice towards the &quot;terroni&quot; was rampant, as southerners mostly lived in poverty, forming their own communities and not speaking the same language. Turin is also considered the most magical city in the country, full of symbolism and relics. It also hosts one of the oldest Egyptian Museums, if not the oldest. But why mages? It's time for rebuilding in the magical community. It is way too easy thinking that only the Seers were aiding the Fascist Regime. Also, we didn't undergo something like the Nuremberg Trials. Other than a few exceptions, many Fascists were pardoned (even if Fascism is still <i>unconstitutional</i>). What happened to Fascist mages? Were they also pardoned? Were they banished? And what is the state of the Hegemonic Ministry? (In Italy they probably suffered nothing more than a slap on the wrist, but they won't use the <i>fasci combattenti</i> as a symbol, <i>for</i> <i>obvious reasons</i>).<br /> I have more issues with Mummy, since I know very little of the gameline. Turin is <i>perfect</i> as a city for mummies, but I don't know if the era is a good fit.<br /> <b>\u2022 1968-1982, The Years of Lead [Hunter]:I</b>n a word: political terrorism. Far right groups vs far left groups vs the government (we had the most ridiculous attempt at a golpe in the '70s, look it up), with just a hint of mafia. It's an era of strife, of change. Divorce was finally legalized, songwriters were all the rage (and most of the songs were politically tinted). How can a cell survive in an era like this? How do supernaturals manage under all that surveillance?<br /> ... maybe Demons could be added for a crossover era, but then we'll have a carbon copy of the Cold War one.<br /> <br /> Lots can also be done with the Muslim conquest of Sicily (Changeling/Mummy, maybe?).</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":3765,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","user":"SNESferatu","date":". 05-07-2017, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom"